body:
`validateSignature` only removes `KeyInfo` when `X509Certificate` is absent:

```go
if el.FindElement("./Signature/KeyInfo/X509Data/X509Certificate") == nil {
    // remove KeyInfo
}
```

An attacker can include a dummy `X509Certificate` to prevent removal, then pack the `KeyInfo` with their own key material. If `goxmldsig` validates against the embedded key rather than the metadata certificate store, the signature check is bypassed.

The fix always strips `KeyInfo` so that signature validation relies solely on the metadata-provided certificates. Also restructures the validation loop to try each trusted certificate individually, since `goxmldsig` only auto-selects a cert when the store has exactly one root.

Fix: [`fix/issue-10`](../tree/fix/issue-10)
